          "Freeman's stakeholder theory argues for obligations to all parties materially affected by the firm, while shareholder primacy restricts obligations to shareholders. In your current business, who are all the parties materially affected by your decisions? When their interests conflict with your financial interests, what framework do you actually use to navigate the conflict — and is that the framework you want to be using?",
